GraphMolecule construction and the staging of reaction examples informed the
write-on design. All animation code and assets in Molecule Studio are original.

Molecule Studio implements the vector bond and label rendering, fit, highlight
and reveal logic, reaction arrows and spacing, and tetrahedral wedge/dash
assignment from the ligand order recorded by chematic. The tetrahedral rules
follow section 3.8.2 of OpenSMILES (https://opensmiles.org/opensmiles.html).
The explicit water depiction uses the measured H–O–H angle reported by the
NIST CCCBDB (https://cccbdb.nist.gov/expangle2x.asp?all=0&descript=aHOH).
The host supplies the glyph outlines through shape-text. The bundle includes
no fonts.
